(4262440, 611663, 39057, '<td valign="top">This is real man...the closer objects will blur more that the objects in the distance. Objects in the center will not blur at all.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by whiteflyer:</b></div><hr/><i> Good image, but the blur looks to have been done in software as the clouds not blurred and the distance trees are still sharp, is this basic editing or an effect of using a fish eye lens ? </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'This is real man...the closer objects will blur more that the objects in the distance. Objects in the center will not blur at all. Originally posted by whiteflyer: Good image, but the blur looks to have been done in software as the clouds not blurred and the distance trees are still sharp, is this basic editing or an effect of using a fish eye lens ? ', '2007-11-21 09:15:56.000000', NULL, 0),
