(4262691, 612886, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by digitalknight:</b></div><hr/><i> I have spent entirely too much money on a studio - if I had your creativity and flair for simple elegant composition, I might have saved enough money on gear to fly my wife and I over there to meet you and the stern guy!<br/> <br/>LOVE the lines in this.  Did I mention who I want to be when I grow up?  (but with a different hair cut).<br/> <br/>You are terrific at this - well, terrific in lots of ways.  Congrats on an excellent photo - </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''d love the stern guy and he''d love you. So start saving!!</td>', 'Originally posted by digitalknight: I have spent entirely too much money on a studio - if I had your creativity and flair for simple elegant composition, I might have saved enough money on gear to fly my wife and I over there to meet you and the stern guy! LOVE the lines in this.  Did I mention who I want to be when I grow up?  (but with a different hair cut). You are terrific at this - well, terrific in lots of ways.  Congrats on an excellent photo -   You''d love the stern guy and he''d love you. So start saving!!', '2007-11-21 11:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4262709, 612392, 61315, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the votes and comments! This was taken in natural light on a piece of computer paper and it turned out a bit brighter than I expected and ended up giving the drip a floating appearance. Also, using the macro lens, which I haven''t used a lot yet, I really needed to shoot this at f/9 or more to get a larger DOF and have more of the image in focus. I appreciate all the constructive comments and I''m sure they will help me in the next challenge. <br/>CJ</td>', 'Thanks all for the votes and comments! This was taken in natural light on a piece of computer paper and it turned out a bit brighter than I expected and ended up giving the drip a floating appearance. Also, using the macro lens, which I haven''t used a lot yet, I really needed to shoot this at f/9 or more to get a larger DOF and have more of the image in focus. I appreciate all the constructive comments and I''m sure they will help me in the next challenge. CJ', '2007-11-21 11:28:15.000000', NULL, 0),
