(4263902, 611663, 67237, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Debbi:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a great image and even better as you shared the setup with us. BUT, why would this win in a category of "topless with no people" when clearly the no people rule was not followed?<br/>Debbi </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Debbi, your opinnion is based on the challenge name or title.<br/> <br/>It would be great if all of us, dpchallengers, read the challenge DESCRIPTION and not just the title of it. In this case, although the challenge title says "..With No People", the description says "..The photo <b>may not have a person as its main, topless subject</b>.". Senor_Kasper''s photo has a car as it''s main topless subject, so it perfectly fits the challenge description.<br/> <br/>I can''t blame you for the confusion though, since there is a contradiction in the wording of the name and the description of this challenge. Maybe the SC could consider posting a copy the DESCRIPTION, in red fonts, in the voting page.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-21 22:41:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Debbi: This is a great image and even better as you shared the setup with us. BUT, why would this win in a category of "topless with no people" when clearly the no people rule was not followed?Debbi   Debbi, your opinnion is based on the challenge name or title. It would be great if all of us, dpchallengers, read the challenge DESCRIPTION and not just the title of it. In this case, although the challenge title says "..With No People", the description says "..The photo may not have a person as its main, topless subject.". Senor_Kasper''s photo has a car as it''s main topless subject, so it perfectly fits the challenge description. I can''t blame you for the confusion though, since there is a contradiction in the wording of the name and the description of this challenge. Maybe the SC could consider posting a copy the DESCRIPTION, in red fonts, in the voting page.', '2007-11-21 22:35:42.000000', '2007-11-21 22:41:15.000000', 0),
